  "titleEn": "Directions",
  "grammarTip": "To give directions, use the imperative: 'skrenuti' (to turn) becomes skreni (informal) or skrenite (formal / plural) — Skreni lijevo! (Turn left!) Skrenite desno! (Turn right!). Many place prepositions — iza (behind), pored (next to), blizu (near), između (between), kod (at/by) — govern the genitive case: iza semafora (behind the traffic light), pored raskrsnice (next to the intersection), kod stanice (at the station).",
